0412BF             2431*   ; Build the fine camera local-to-world orientation for roll zero. This is the
0412BF             2432*   ; closed form Ry(y)*Rx(x), avoiding the coarse general Euler rotators while
0412BF             2433*   ; keeping the retained matrix byte-consistent with the emitted fine angles.
0412BF             2434*   ;
0412BF             2435*   ; inputs:
0412BF             2436*   ;   ix -> destination matrix
0412BF             2437*   ;   iy -> Pingo-angle vec3; z is ignored and must semantically be zero
0412BF             2438*   ; outputs:
0412BF             2439*   ;   matrix = Ry(y)*Rx(x)
0412BF             2440*   ;   carry clear on success
0412BF             2441*   ; destroys:
0412BF             2442*   ;   af, af', bc, de, hl, bc', de', hl'
0412BF             2443*   ; preserves:
0412BF             2444*   ;   ix, iy
0412BF             2445*   ;
0412BF             2446*   ; This helper is used inside the camera's whole-state transaction. A
0412BF             2447*   ; theoretical multiply failure may leave a partial destination for that
0412BF             2448*   ; outer transaction to restore.
0412BF             2449*   p3d_camera_mat3_from_euler_fine16:
